  "goodToKnow": "Die Gräueltat is an atrocity, usually in war or under dictatorship. Since the 1996 spelling reform it's written with äu (Gräuel, from Grauen, horror) instead of the older Greuel. Der Gräuel means abomination: Das ist mir ein Gräuel (I detest it). International courts, such as the one in The Hague, prosecute war crimes and crimes against humanity. Plural: die Gräueltaten."
